course: dictionary
lesson: 8282
title: Riot and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A riot is a violent, noisy disturbance by a crowd of people in a public place. «Civil unrest means riots and protests» shows that a riot is one kind of trouble that happens when many people are angry at once.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Violent and noisy tell you this is not a calm gathering. Ask what would fit: if you swap in "a loud, angry crowd breaking things", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Riot has other meanings too. «The party was a riot» means it was great fun, not violent at all. «A riot of colour» means a very bright mix of colours. The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Historians think the famous riots of people shouting «give us our eleven days» probably never happened. A story can be famous and still be doubtful, so when you read about a riot, ask whether the source can be trusted.
fact: A riot is a violent, noisy disturbance by a crowd of people in a public place.
fact: As a verb, to riot means to take part in such a disturbance.
fact: «She's a riot!» is informal and means she is very funny and great fun.
fact: «A riot of colour» means a very bright mix of colours.
fact: «Run riot» means to behave wildly without control, or to grow wildly.
exercise: «The party was a riot, and everyone laughed all night.» What does riot mean here? | Quiet and calm | Violent and angry | A bright mix of colours | *Great fun
exercise: «The garden plants began to run riot after the rain.» What does run riot mean? | To stop growing completely | To paint the fence in bright colours | *To grow wildly, without control
exercise: «Police in riot gear tried to stop the crowd.» What is riot gear most likely to be? | *Protective clothing and equipment for stopping violent crowds | Clothes for a fancy party | Swimming costumes
test: What does «a riot of colour» mean? | *A very bright mix of colours | A violent crowd of painters | Dull, grey paint
test: In «The crowd began to riot after the match», what kind of word is riot? | A noun, the name of a thing | A colour | *A verb, an action word
exam: Historians think the famous riots of people shouting «give us our eleven days» probably never happened. What does this teach you? | *A famous story can still be doubtful, so check the source | Famous stories are only about colours | Every famous story is always true
